WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:07.279
With a total gross approaching $750 million,
Suicide Squad proved to be one of the DCEU's

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.530
most successful films.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.800
So no matter how few stars critics gave the
first one, we know a second one's coming.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.080
Here's all the rumors and spoilers leaked
so far about the sequel.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.480
James Gunn was infamously, temporarily booted
from the director's chair of the upcoming

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.240
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3 over controversy
regarding years-old tweets.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.220
Marvel's initial loss proved to be Warner
Bros.' gain.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:34.900
In October 2018, news dropped that Gunn was
tapped to write the sequel to Suicide Squad.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.400
In January 2019, The Hollywood Reporter broke
the news that the Marvel Studios exile was

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.820
negotiating to direct the villainous squad's
next adventure, too.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.700
Gunn is planning a "completely new take" on
Task Force X, and it may not be a direct sequel

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.840
in strictest sense.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.520
Speaking to JoBlo, Aquaman and Shazam! producer
Peter Safran spilled a few details:

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.200
"First of all, we don't call it Suicide Squad
2 'cause it's a total reboot...It's everything

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.040
you would hope from a James Gunn script."

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:09.360
Gunn's film will be titled The Suicide Squad
and will "relaunch" the franchise with a "mostly

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.140
all-new cast of characters and actors."

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.840
Gunn has a large toybox of characters from
which to choose.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.720
The Suicide Squad comic has featured dozens
of different DC supervillains and there are

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.820
plenty of Squad regulars still waiting to
appear on the big screen.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.720
THR said The Suicide Squad will be "rooted
in Gunn's vibe," which most likely means we

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.240
can expect the same unique blend of action,
humor, and drama the director brought to his

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.280
two Guardians of the Galaxy films.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.640
"In the beginning, in the script stage, I
create it all in my head, and then it's simply

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.520
a matter of trying to make the movie look
like what's in my head."

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:49.060
No other Guardians of the Galaxy star vocally
disagreed with Disney's decision to fire Gunn

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.940
as as much as Dave Bautista.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.190
He threatened to break his contract for Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3 if Disney didn't use

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.120
Gunn's script.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.580
It's no surprise that almost as soon as it
was announced Gunn would be working on The

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.080
Suicide Squad, Bautista was congratulating
him on Twitter.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:11.020
Bautista's tweet inspired a quick response,
with fans speculating who the former WWE star

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:11.560
should play.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:17.140
One of the more common nominations was Bane,
the ruthless strongman who famously broke

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:21.980
Batman's back and was first portrayed in live
action by Tom Hardy in Christopher Nolan's

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.060
The Dark Knight Rises.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.800
While the Bane of the comics was only briefly
a member of Suicide Squad, he was a regular

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.640
in the comic book Secret Six, which also featured
supervillains as protagonists.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:38.780
According to Collider, Peacemaker, a violent
pacifist who believes in peace so much he's

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.450
willing to kill to achieve it, is the role
Gunn wants for the Guardians of the Galaxy

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:43.940
star.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.980
When Peacemaker first appeared on the comic
book stands, it was as part of the now-defunct

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.500
Charlton Comics, whose superhero properties
were acquired by DC Comics.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:58.340
He's also one of the Charlton refugees writer
Alan Moore wanted to use for Watchmen.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:04.240
When DC editor Dick Giordano told Moore that
DC wanted to save the Charlton characters

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:09.170
for other things, Moore replaced the Charlton
superheroes with his own altered versions

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:09.660
of them.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.980
Peacemaker's replacement was The Comedian,
whose murder sets off the events of Watchmen.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:21.060
In January 2019, The Hollywood Reporter confirmed
a scheduled release month for the relaunch:

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.840
August 2021.

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.730
Since Suicide Squad's 2016 release, there
have been plenty of questions about whether

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.560
there would even be a sequel.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.760
Writing duties have changed hands several
times and it was never clear whether David

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.940
Ayer would return to the director's chair.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:42.060
As early as February 2017, rumors were circulating
that Mel Gibson was being courted to helm

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:42.700
the sequel.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:48.120
While Gunn is confirmed as writer, and possibly
director, of the follow-up film, it shouldn't

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.940
be too surprising that there will ultimately
be five years between the first and second

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:53.440
movies.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:57.520
It may be that the extra time will work in
The Suicide Squad's favor.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.300
With Gunn reportedly pursuing a new direction
with a largely new cast, the added time may

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:06.620
allow memories of the first movie to fade
and pave the way for a fresh start.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:13.740
In February 2019, Forbes reported that in
spite of the character's unquestionable popularity,

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:17.920
Margot Robbie wouldn't be reprising her role
as Harley Quinn in The Suicide Squad.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:23.540
In its piece about the state of the DCEU,
Forbes wrote that Quinn was being jettisoned

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:28.520
from the Suicide Squad franchise as part of
Gunn's "rethinking of the property" and the

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.260
"new flavor" he wanted to bring to it.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:34.540
Robbie's days as Harley Quinn aren't over,
though, as she will be appearing in the upcoming

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.500
Birds of Prey and the Fantabulous Emancipation
of One Harley Quinn.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:40.160
"We're bad guys.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.560
It's what we do."

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.260
But that wasn't the end of the story.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:49.740
The week after publishing the story online,
Forbes contributor Mark Hughes posted a correction,

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:53.060
saying that he had been wrong about no home
for Harley in the follow-up.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.020
Hughes wrote,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.700
"I have learned from sources close to production
that in fact…[Robbie as Harley Quinn] is

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:03.560
indeed expected to appear in James Gunn's
The Suicide Squad, which is expected to begin

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.200
production later this year."

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:11.740
In late February 2019, Variety reported that
Will Smith opted to not reprise his role as

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:17.200
Floyd Lawton, a.k.a. Deadshot, the sharpshooter
assassin Smith played in the first Suicide

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:17.700
Squad.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:21.460
Variety says there's no bad blood between
Smith and Warner Bros.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.720
Instead, it looks like scheduling is to blame.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.380
"Pleasure doin' business wit' you."

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.260
Warner Bros. was hoping Smith would be one
of the actors to return.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.600
If Deadshot is missing in action in the new
film, it will be somewhat fitting.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:38.820
In the comics, he's proven to be one of the
most consistent presences in the various Task

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:43.180
Force X rosters, but they're much more fluid
than other comics super-teams.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:48.360
A Suicide Squad movie with no Deadshot might
be regrettable, but the character isn't as

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.480
integral as Chris Evans' Captain America would
be to an Avengers movie.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:58.480
ScreenRant has proposed a promising fix: plucking
Joe Manganiello's Deathstroke out of DCEU

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.720
limbo to replace Smith.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:03.960
Or maybe Smith will be replaced with a new
Deadshot.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:09.080
THR reported that MCU veteran Idris Elba was
in talks to replace Smith in the part.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:14.960
According to the story, Elba met with James
Gunn in early March 2019 and the discussion

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:19.220
"went so swimmingly" that Elba was ready to
dive right into negotiations.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.540
It's an interesting development, particularly
considering some of the less-than-glowing

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:29.320
comments that surfaced from Elba while playing
the Asgardian gatekeeper Heimdall in Marvel

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:29.820
Studios' films.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:36.120
Elba played Heimdall for all three Thor films,
Avengers: Age of Ultron, and finally Avengers:

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:41.280
Infinity War, when his character met his end
at the gauntlet-wearing hand of Thanos.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:45.860
Elba raised a few eyebrows when he expressed
frustration with working on Marvel movies

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.160
in a 2014 interview with the Telegraph.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:53.900
If Elba's willing to jump back into the world
of superheroes so soon after Thanos liberated

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:58.560
him from the role of Heimdall, then that chat
with Gunn really must have gone "swimmingly."

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:04.600
In the same story that announced Idris Elba
was gunning for the role of Deadshot, THR

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:09.810
also cited sources telling them Joel Kinnaman
would not be reprising his role as Task Force

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:10.980
X watchdog Rick Flag.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:16.340
The story said that while most of the cast
of 2016's Suicide Squad would be set aside

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:20.860
for newer blood, there were three characters
in particular that were expected to return:

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.220
Deadshot, Harley Quinn and Flag.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.020
But sources conflict.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:29.420
Some say Kinnaman is expected to return, and
others expect the character will be cut from

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.000
the team.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.740
"When the shootin' starts, and it will, you'll
cut and run."

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:39.340
What would be interesting is if Rick Flag
does appear in the sequel and Kinnaman steps

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:42.580
down from the role, forcing filmmakers to
recast the part.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:47.760
With Deadshot recast and potentially Flag,
eventually we might just be able to call the

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:50.070
sequel Suicide Squad: The Recasting.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:56.250
The question of just how "soft" a reboot James
Gunn's The Suicide Squad will be seems to

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:01.150
get more complicated with every related news
story, and it grew a little more complex with

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:06.700
the news of at least one alumnus of 2016's
Suicide Squad returning to Task Force X.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:12.440
Talking to Business Insider in March 2019,
Jai Courtney confirmed he would reprise the

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.860
role of Captain Boomerang in the upcoming
film.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:19.780
Courtney said he wasn't free to reveal too
many details, but added that The Suicide Squad

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:23.760
would be shooting in "a few months' time"
and that he was glad to be back in the fold.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:24.600
He said:

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.580
"I'm happy, it's going to be fun.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.260
It will be different, for sure, but it's going
to be great."

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:34.160
The news is something of a surprise as the
rumblings until now have suggested that while

00:08:34.169 --> 00:08:39.519
the studio was hoping for the returns of Will
Smith, Margot Robbie, and Viola Davis to their

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:42.020
roles, the rest of the cast would likely be
replaced.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:48.040
Collider has reportedly gotten word of who
some of Task Force X's other members would

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:48.540
be.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:53.120
One shouldn't come as much of a surprise to
fans of the Suicide Squad comic.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:58.350
King Shark, the savage man-shark hybrid, was
one of the characters predicted, and the choice

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.420
makes sense.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:05.580
When DC rebooted its entire superhero comic
book universe in 2011 with "The New 52," King

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:08.380
Shark became one of the Squad's first members.

00:09:08.569 --> 00:09:14.200
Likewise, he accompanied the Squad and Batman
in the 2014 animated film Batman: Assault

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:14.960
on Arkham.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:20.410
The character also appeared prominently on
CW's The Flash in the episode "King Shark

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.780
vs. Gorilla Grodd."

00:09:22.249 --> 00:09:27.240
If Collider's report is true, some of the
other characters prove Gunn isn't exactly

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:30.080
pulling from DC's A-list of bad guys.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:34.600
The site says Suicide Squad's roster will
include two Batman villains who fall squarely

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:40.050
in the D-list: a female version of the Ratcatcher,
a former exterminator who commits crimes with

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:45.390
an army of rats she controls, and the Polka-Dot
Man, who can turn the polka dots on his costume

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.390
into gadgets.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:51.680
The beginning of 2019 was a good time for
writer/director James Gunn.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:56.720
In Mid-March, Deadline broke possibly the
best news of the year thus far: Disney had

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:00.400
rehired him as the director for Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:06.819
While most MCU fans were likely over the moon
at hearing the news, fans of DC Comics adaptations

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:08.380
might have been a little concerned.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:13.460
After all, if Gunn was back on Guardians,
did that mean he'd drop The Suicide Squad

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.540
like a bad habit and run back home?

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:20.740
According to Aquaman and Shazam! producer
Peter Safran, the answer to that is a definitive

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:21.240
no.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.240
Speaking to JoBlo, Safran said,

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:28.520
"It was all handled incredibly elegantly and
everybody knows on both sides that Suicide

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.560
Squad is the priority today."

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:35.739
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, Safran said,
will be Gunn's next film after The Suicide

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:36.240
Squad.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:41.900
That means, according to ScreenRant, Guardians
fans will have to wait until 2023 at the earliest

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.620
for the next entry in the series.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.140
"This is no respectable establishment.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.540
What do you expect us to do while we wait?"

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:54.839
According to Production Weekly, The Suicide
Squad will be under the working title El Dorado

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.040
once it enters production.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.700
There's no indication exactly why El Dorado
was chosen, or if it's at all relevant to

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:01.660
the film's story.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:06.839
The name is usually associated with a legendary
city in South America whose very structures

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.199
and roads were said to be made of solid gold.

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:13.600
The city has been the subject of numerous
films, and it's a popular subject in music

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.160
as well.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:19.360
Everyone from the '80s punk band Agent Orange
to metal gods Iron Maiden and alt-rockers

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:22.500
Death Cab for Cutie has recorded an "El Dorado"
song.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:25.100
Shakira named her 2017 album El Dorado.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:30.440
Of course, as a working title, El Dorado doesn't
necessarily need to have any connection whatsoever

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:35.429
with the film's story, though it'd be pretty
great if it means Gunn plans to make The Suicide

00:11:35.429 --> 00:11:36.460
Squad an animated musical.

